 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: «*riǵl al-ǵawzā’*» is printed in italics, with the acute on both g, the bar over the a and the apostrophe of the hamzah; «β» is Greek. In «Orionis» the r and the i stand 1.9 points apart (the word spaces of the line are 3.1–6.1 points); read Orionis.",
  "col_left L2: the end of the tail of the italic 9 of «*179*» stands apart (2.0 by 2.2 points, on the baseline), like a point; it is not a point. The point after the 9 follows it.",
  "col_left L3: «*ar-rishā’*» is printed in italics, with the bar over the a and the apostrophe of the hamzah.",
  "col_left L8: the t of «Cataneus» is printed without its crossbar, like l (its height is that of a t); read t.",
  "col_left L10: «*Romaka-siddhānta*» is printed in italics, with the bar over the a.",
  "col_left L11: the a and the n of «Romani» are printed run together; read Romani. «ar-Rūm» has the bar over the u.",
  "col_left L13: a piece of the diagonal of the z of «Ronzevalle» (1.6 by 1.7 points) stands apart on the baseline, like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left L20: «Rudloff» is printed with the ff ligature.",
  "col_left L21: the comma after «II» is printed short (1.7 by 2.5 points, its foot 0.5 point below the baseline).",
  "col_left L23: «ar-Rūm» has the bar over the u.",
  "col_left L24, L25: a blank line separates the names in R from those in S.",
  "col_left L30, L31: «*sa‘d al-akhbiyah*», «*sa‘d bula‘*», «*sa‘d adh-dhā-*» and «*sa‘d as-su‘ūd*» are printed in italics, with the sign of ‘ayn (six times), the bar over the a of «adh-dhā-» and over the second u of «as-su‘ūd»; «*biḥ*» has the dot under the italic h.",
  "col_left L32: «Shādhān» has the bars over both a.",
  "col_left L33: «Ṣādiq» has the dot under the S and the bar over the a (the bar touching the a); «Muḥ.» has the dot under the h.",
  "col_left L44: «*sahm as-sa‘ādah*» is printed in italics, with the sign of ‘ayn and the bar over the second a.",
  "col_left L45: «Saḥnūn» has the dot under the h and the bar over the u; the lower terminal of its S stands apart like a point; it is not a point. In «‘Othmān», after the sign of ‘ayn, the O, the t and the h are printed heavier and crowded, the h running into the m; a small hooked mark (1.8 by 2.3 points) under the left side of the O, from 0.8 point above to 1.5 points below the baseline, is not transcribed. The a has its bar. «al-Wānsharīshī» has the bars over the a and over both i (3.5, 2.4 and 2.3 points long), read at 8,000 dpi.",
  "col_left L33, L45, col_right L3, L7, L20, L27: the dots under the h of «Muḥ.» (twice), «Saḥnūn» and «Aḥmad» and under the H of «al-Ḥasan» and «Ḥiyyā» (1.4 points across) hang from the foot serifs of the letter, read at 6,000 dpi; they are dots, not breves.",
  "col_right L3: «Ṣā‘id» has the dot under the S, the bar over the a and the sign of ‘ayn; «al-Ḥasan» has the dot under the H; «al-Andalusī» has the bar over the last i (2.3 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_right L5: «as-Sa‘īdi» has the bar over the first i (1.9 by 1.1 points); its last i has a round dot (1.2 by 1.0 points), with a speck (0.5 by 0.5 point) beside it, read at 8,000 dpi; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L7: «as-Salāwī» has the bars over the a (touching the letter) and over the last i; its hyphen is printed as a small point at mid height (1.2 by 0.7 points). «Aḥmad» has the dot under the h. «an-Nāṣirī» has the bar over the a, the dot under the s, a round dot on the first i (1.6 by 1.6 points) and the bar over the last i (2.6 by 1.1 points); its hyphen is printed thick, as a blot (3.4 by 2.2 points). Both are read as hyphens.",
  "col_right L8: «Ṣalībā» has the dot under the S, a short bar over the i (1.8 by 1.1 points, flatter than the round dots of this type) and the bar over the a.",
  "col_right L12: the e of «Pater» is printed broken, its loop open and its two sides apart; read e.",
  "col_right L13: «as-Sam‘ānī» has the sign of ‘ayn and the bars over the a and over the last i (2.6 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_right L14: «*sammà*» is printed in italics, with the grave on the last a.",
  "col_right L17: «‘Alī» begins with the sign of ‘ayn and has the bar over the i; «Abū» has the bar over the u; «’ṭ-ṭayyib» begins with the apostrophe of elision and has the dots under both t (1.6 by 1.1 and 1.6 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L18: «*sanah ‘aǵamiyyah*» is printed in italics, with the sign of ‘ayn and the acute on the g. A speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) at mid height between «202» and «n.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L20: «as-Sanūsī» has the bars over the u and the last i; its hyphen is printed short (2.0 by 1.1 points). «Yūsuf» has the bar over the u.",
  "col_right L21: «*śara*» is printed in italics, with the acute on the s, read at 8,000 dpi.",
  "col_right L22: «*aṣ-ṣarfah*» is printed in italics, with the dots under both s; «β» is Greek.",
  "col_right L23: «*al-muqātil*» is printed in italics, with the bar over the a.",
  "col_right L26, L27: «Abrāhām» has the bars over both a, and «Ḥiyyā» the bar over the a; the bars touch the letters, read at 5,000 dpi.",
  "col_right L28: «Schaffner» is printed with the ff ligature.",
  "col_right L30: «Shādhān» has the bars over both a.",
  "col_right L32: «σχηματισμοί» is Greek, with the acute on the last ι (the accent joined to the letter), read at 8,000 dpi. «figurae» is printed with the fi ligature.",
  "col_right L33: the right end of the foot of the L of «{sc:lxiv}» stands apart (1.9 by 2.0 points, on the baseline), like a point; it is not a point. A speck (0.6 by 0.4 point) at mid height between its X and I is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L41: the upper and the lower ball of the 3 of «232» stand apart from the figure, like a colon between the 2 and the 3, read at 8,000 dpi; read 232.",
  "col_left, col_right: in this type the ball terminals of the figures 3, 5 and 9 and of s are joined to them by hairlines that often did not print; on this page 60 loose pieces are listed by loose_pieces.py (with the real points). Low on the line like points stand the lower balls of the 3s of «37» and «39» (L4), «43» (L5), «203» (L11), «36» (L17), «213» and «293» (L20), «213» (L26), «39» (L27), «193» (L28), «324» (L29), «38» (L33), «306» (L42), «326» (L43), «338-339» (L44, twice), «334» (R12), «333» (R25), «43» (R36) and «193» (R38), a ball of a 5 of «355» (L29), the tails of the 9s of «290» and «291» (R46) and the lower terminal of the s of «Robertus» (L8). None of them is a point."
